{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788032073548045001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"presolar-finable-binturong","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3db665c861b42e64dc029128bd8d6baa278234ad0288bc0c40a7c0170363491c","event_uuid":"0892cb65-63d3-412e-8874-b6638332f266","position":{"commit_sha":"342d34cb6f39224b3dfa333541dda533f12baa27","position":"1788029145159590662-0892cb65-63d3-412e-8874-b6638332f266"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d8d7170980b53cf98fa9a8e9e19ebffe6ab54bd7fabffe7db41db2824705c23d","event_uuid":"c06b763d-6893-4c66-b07b-7808df5c6b45","position":{"commit_sha":"b6a8a397f61a92a99b610b8b3d91484f8ebad117","position":"1788029256637507593-c06b763d-6893-4c66-b07b-7808df5c6b45"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"85a0de502125af58e378fb1d23604019a78d12a1e064c72660fedd1635fb01c7","event_uuid":"5622bbb6-0599-4dca-a150-f773a9a7a9a7","position":{"commit_sha":"403212682782cfcc53a230bc01c9d8457a841e21","position":"1788029265578135235-5622bbb6-0599-4dca-a150-f773a9a7a9a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f78bfc0fe53c321aae0b6ed1e6cd28520c20b968fb8e8015004b66406b790012","event_uuid":"17c5467e-1eea-429c-b9fc-c64aab31bee3","position":{"commit_sha":"47715f277401f4676b7eae6478616d09501a3563","position":"1788029273663337165-17c5467e-1eea-429c-b9fc-c64aab31bee3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e37e6cd058ef912326aa5cdc58fefa27eb6ed81f73d4699564d68962e97e92b8","event_uuid":"2b4427db-d441-4ba5-bc15-0eb43f9f870c","position":{"commit_sha":"0cb5e15208c22629bec88a26fc3de4b9089bdfc0","position":"1788029594158607400-2b4427db-d441-4ba5-bc15-0eb43f9f870c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029145159590662,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c06b763d-6893-4c66-b07b-7808df5c6b45","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb"},{"link_uuid":"5622bbb6-0599-4dca-a150-f773a9a7a9a7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4c80-edd3-20f1-4dff"},{"link_uuid":"17c5467e-1eea-429c-b9fc-c64aab31bee3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 2 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`, questions in `verify_models.py`, prompts `reviewers/plan_review_verifier*.md`, `temperature: 0`, standard class = Sonnet on Bedrock) is the cheapest LLM pass (~$0.5/review uncached, ~1 call with ~12 requests) and the one whose questions most directly set validity/impact. A question or prompt change can be measured by re-verifying the *stored* Pass-1 findings and comparing to the stored answers — no Opus needed. `verify_findings(findings, context, run_chunk=…)` already exposes the pure seam; `plan-review-verifier.eval.yaml` has no `run_case` arm yet.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py`:\n\n- Sample selection: deterministic stratified sample from the corpus (strata: verdict, leaf/container, finding count bucket, project overlay/store, `impact_model_version`), size N given on the command line, seed fixed; only `verified` rows (reconstructed plan text) are eligible; only rows whose `provider_provenance.ran_model` is the current standard-class model.\n- For each sampled review: build the verifier context from reconstructed plan text + stored findings (`finding, criteria, evidence, impact, location`), run the candidate verifier (prompt/questions from a candidate path; default = current) through the production `PydanticAIRunner` pinned to the standard class on Bedrock, collect `{binary, severity_attributes}`.\n- Compare to stored answers: per-question agreement (Cohen κ and raw agreement per graded binary and veto question; per-attribute agreement for severity attributes), validity/impact/priority distribution shift, then hand both answer sets to Tier 0 for the downstream verdict/label metrics.\n- A **reproduction run** (candidate = current) is the first commissioning run: its agreement is the verifier noise floor at temperature 0 and is stored with the labels.\n- All calls go through the budget ledger pre-flight (estimate = stored `metrics` tokens × current price × N) and record the model id per result.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py`, `sampling.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py` (add the verifier `run_case` arm)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier1-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier1.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: sampling is deterministic for a seed and respects strata; a `FakeRunner` returning canned verifications yields the expected per-question agreement table; a run whose pre-flight estimate exceeds the ledger allocation is refused before any call; a result with a non-standard-class model id is rejected at diff time. Live (commissioning, ≤$40): the reproduction run on N=60.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier1 --candidate <path> --n N` produces per-question agreement, distribution shift and downstream Tier-0 metrics for a stratified sample; checked by one generated report.\n- [ ] The reproduction run (current questions) is recorded with its per-question agreement as the Pass-2 noise floor; checked by the report and the labels file.\n- [ ] Every call in the run is priced in the ledger and uses the Bedrock standard-class model id; checked by the ledger rows for the run.\n- [ ] Commissioning spend for this ticket ≤ $40; checked by the ledger.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py","reason":"Pass-2 replay"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/sampling.py","reason":"stratified sampler"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"verifier run_case arm"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"generated reports"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier1.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","4c80-edd3-20f1-4dff"],["depends_on","5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb"],["depends_on","efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-1","pass-2"],"ticket_id":"53ab-bdf6-de1c-4bb1","ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-1 harness: replay Pass-2 impact/validity questions on stored Pass-1 findings (Sonnet via Bedrock, budgeted)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0892cb65-63d3-412e-8874-b6638332f266","c06b763d-6893-4c66-b07b-7808df5c6b45","5622bbb6-0599-4dca-a150-f773a9a7a9a7","17c5467e-1eea-429c-b9fc-c64aab31bee3","2b4427db-d441-4ba5-bc15-0eb43f9f870c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788032073548045001,"uuid":"34696a9a-123c-429c-b264-0e120c96758c"}